1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,640
She sold a bank four million customers who didn't exist.

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:07,100
Charlie Javice started a website called Frank in twenty sixteen.

3
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:12,000
It helped students fill out the giant form you need for college financial aid.

4
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:15,380
By twenty twenty-one, big banks wanted to buy it.

5
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:18,640
And she told them Frank had four and a quarter million users.

6
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:21,820
The SEC says the real number was fewer than three hundred thousand.

7
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:24,980
Hit like if you'd have believed her.

8
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:30,460
So what did the bank, JPMorgan, do? The smart thing. It asked to see the customer list.

9
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:33,940
Here's the problem. There was no list of four million people.

10
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:39,440
The SEC says she first asked her own engineer to make fake data. But he said no.

11
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:45,640
So she and a coworker hired a data science professor, who generated over four million fake customers.

12
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:48,280
According to the bank's lawsuit, he was paid about eighteen thousand dollars.

13
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,340
Send this to the friend who rounds up their follower count.

14
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:57,840
The bank got the list, and JPMorgan paid one hundred seventy-five million dollars for Frank.

15
00:00:57,840 --> 00:01:01,200
That's about five hundred eighty dollars for every real user.

16
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:05,680
Later, the bank tried reaching those customers. And the list? It fell apart.

17
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:08,380
Follow if you love it when the math catches up.

18
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:12,120
In twenty twenty-five, a jury convicted her on all four counts.

19
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:16,240
She was sentenced to eighty-five months in prison, a little over seven years.

20
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:20,560
And she was ordered to pay back two hundred eighty-seven and a half million dollars.

21
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:24,440
Four million, or three hundred thousand? Which would you have checked?

